  "opis": "Same model (Qwen3.8 27B), same task (an HTML report from 144 JSON files of our own measurements, 22 checks, raport-check), Pi, LM Studio, effort medium, 3 runs per variant, model reloaded before every run. Variants: BARE (Pi without extensions) and CONTEXT-MODE (context-mode 1.0.169). Input (prompt tokens, all requests of a run): BARE 35.6k–168.3k, CONTEXT-MODE 113.3k–397.0k — the ranges overlap. No saving: every CONTEXT-MODE request carried 7.0k more prompt tokens; the first one started at 8.6k against 1.6k (15 tools instead of 4). With one run each, run 1 would have shown the opposite (CONTEXT-MODE 113.3k, BARE 168.3k). The model used context-mode's own tools in 1 of 3 runs. In every run it read the data with one script; the largest tool output was 7,525 characters, so there was little to trim. Score of 22: BARE 19, CONTEXT-MODE 21–22; the values were right on all 6 pages, the BARE misses were the layout of the answer. 3 runs each: an observation on one model and one task, not a rule.",
